# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<script setup>
const emit = defineEmits([`click`, "change"]);
emit(`click`);
emit("keydown");
(emit)?.("CHANGE");
</script>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid-script-setup.vue:3:27 lint/nursery/noVueShadowNativeEvents ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This component event has the same name as the browser event click.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <script setup>
  > 3 │ const emit = defineEmits([`click`, "change"]);
      │                           ^^^^^^^
    4 │ emit(`click`);
    5 │ emit("keydown");
  
  i It is easy to mistake for the browser event, but it works differently: listeners receive the value passed to emit instead of an Event object, the event doesn't reach the elements around the component, and modifiers such as .stop don't work on it.
  
  i Rename the event to describe what happened in the component.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

